1. Scope and separate notices
This license applies only to files expressly marked
SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-YunCMS-Commercial and their compiled forms
("Premium Components"). Other YunCMS files and third-party dependencies retain
their own licenses. It does not replace, revoke or restrict permissions already
granted for YunCMS versions or components distributed under the MIT License.

2. One codebase and Community distribution
Yunsoft Software may distribute Community and Premium functionality in the same
source tree, npm packages, Studio bundle and container image. Possession of a
bundle or visibility of Premium source code does not grant production use of
Premium Components. You may download, inspect, build and run the Community
functionality, with Premium Components inactive, and redistribute complete,
unmodified official distributions with all notices and feature controls intact.
You may also redistribute builds that modify only MIT-licensed components,
provided Premium sources, notices and entitlement controls remain intact and
Premium use still requires a valid entitlement. Recompiling unchanged Premium
sources as part of such a build is permitted.
Premium Components are source-available proprietary software, not MIT-licensed
or OSI-approved open-source software. No separate Premium codebase is required.

3. Premium grant
Subject to a valid entitlement issued or expressly authorized by Yunsoft
Software, you may use, reproduce and modify Premium Components internally to
operate the features, production site and associated environments identified by
that entitlement. A YunCMS Premium one-time purchase grants perpetual use for
its licensed production domain without a mandatory recurring license fee.
The canonical domain and its www alias are one site; the CMS API hostname used
only for that same site does not require an additional site license. Independent
production sites/domains require their own entitlements. Local development and
staging hosts must be associated with the licensed site and permitted by the
entitlement. Hosting migrations do not require repurchase of the same site
license; domain transfers follow the documented verification/transfer process.
This license does not impose per-user, per-record or per-API-request fees.

4. Feature entitlements and updates
A purchase authorizes only the Premium features expressly included in its
entitlement. Yunsoft Software can issue or update signed grants for those
features. An administrator may disable an authorized feature but cannot grant
additional commercial rights. Updates to purchased features are included when
made available by Yunsoft Software; no promise to create particular future
features or continue a particular service is made. Separately offered new
products, managed hosting, implementation, priority support and third-party AI
usage are not included unless expressly agreed. This license concerns YunCMS;
it does not grant a YunPanel subscription or waive a separate product's terms.

5. Customer data and operational continuity
Your content and other customer data remain yours. Community features, native
security protections, access to your data and ordinary export/backup rights are
not conditional on a Premium purchase. A missing or unverifiable Premium
entitlement does not authorize deletion of data or shutdown of Community
functionality. Paid remote services and third-party providers retain their own
availability, charging and data-processing terms. No unlimited hosted AI usage
is included in a one-time software license.

6. Restrictions applying only to Premium Components
Except as expressly granted above or required by applicable law, you may not
sell, sublicense, publish modified Premium Components, redistribute them
separately, use them for unlicensed independent production sites, or remove or
bypass entitlement controls to obtain rights you have not purchased. Internal
modifications and integrations for your licensed deployment are permitted.
These restrictions do not apply to MIT-licensed components or otherwise limit
rights granted by third-party licenses. No trademark rights are granted.

7. Termination and statutory rights
A site license is not terminated merely because an optional support service
expires or the licensing service is temporarily unavailable. It can be revoked
following an applicable refund, payment reversal, fraud or material breach.
For a remediable material breach, Yunsoft Software will give notice and a
reasonable opportunity of at least 30 days to remedy before termination.
After lawful termination, cease use of the affected Premium Components;
Community use and your rights in your data continue. Nothing in this license
excludes mandatory consumer, interoperability or other statutory rights.

